From: ImpulseROM <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Bypass the minimum installable target SDK check

The minimum is read from PackageManagerService.MIN_INSTALLABLE_TARGET_SDK; use 0 so
apps built for older SDKs install. Rebased onto One UI 8.5 DZF3, where the check no
longer has a bypass flag register.
---
 smali_classes2/com/android/server/pm/InstallPackageHelper.smali | changed
 1 file changed

--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/pm/InstallPackageHelper.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/pm/InstallPackageHelper.smali
@@ -15639,7 +15639,7 @@
 
     move-result v0
 
-    sget v15, Lcom/android/server/pm/PackageManagerService;->MIN_INSTALLABLE_TARGET_SDK:I
+    const/4 v15, 0x0
 
     if-lt v0, v15, :cond_18
 
